From a562ae4c3838eaeb86d12553185d89632ea91f96 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bohdan Chubuk <chbgdn@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 23:21:42 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 10/12] airoha: an7581: add hotplug script to reload firewall
 on bridge port add

At boot the firewall starts before hostapd creates wireless interfaces
and before DSA ports are enslaved to the bridge. Without a reload fw4
cannot discover them as bridge members and bridge hardware offload via
the PPE will only cover wired-to-wired flows.

The net hotplug event fires when a wireless interface (phy*-ap* or
ap-mld*) appears. If the device is not yet present in the bridge
flowtable, a firewall reload is triggered.

Serialised via flock so concurrent hotplug events (multiple SSIDs)
result in a single reload after all interfaces are up.

Signed-off-by: Bohdan Chubuk <chbgdn@gmail.com>
---
 .../etc/hotplug.d/net/50-fw4-bridge-reload    | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 target/linux/airoha/an7581/base-files/etc/hotplug.d/net/50-fw4-bridge-reload

diff --git a/target/linux/airoha/an7581/base-files/etc/hotplug.d/net/50-fw4-bridge-reload b/target/linux/airoha/an7581/base-files/etc/hotplug.d/net/50-fw4-bridge-reload
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..2a5b2dd3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/target/linux/airoha/an7581/base-files/etc/hotplug.d/net/50-fw4-bridge-reload
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+#!/bin/sh
+
+[ "$ACTION" = "add" ] || exit 0
+
+case "${DEVICENAME}" in
+	phy*-ap*|ap-mld*) ;;
+	*) exit 0 ;;
+esac
+
+nft list flowtable bridge fw4 fb 2>/dev/null | grep -qw "\"${DEVICENAME}\"" && exit 0
+
+(
+	exec 9>/var/lock/fw4-bridge-reload.lock
+	flock -n 9 || exit 0
+	sleep 2
+	/etc/init.d/firewall reload >/dev/null 2>&1
+) &
+
+exit 0

